            "readonly": true,
            "desc": "The last round whose block timestamp is at or before `target` (seconds since the epoch): the state \"as of\" that\nmoment, as reti-ghost-sdk's `RoundClock.roundAt`. Searches from `minRound` (at least 1) to the query's round: a\n`target` before `minRound` gives `minRound`, one at or after the query round's timestamp gives the query round.\n\nEach step is a Newton step from the window of rounds the program reads (the 1,001 rounds ending at the round it\nreads as the latest), at that window's own block time. A step that lands outside the bracket interpolates between\nits ends instead, and one that doesn't halve the distance to the target in time bisects next. A read outside the\nwindow seeks there, centred on it; its two ends tighten the bracket too. Logs the result.",
            "events": [],
            "recommendations": {}
        }
    ],
